</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Details of Theoretical Analysis</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First recall the theoretical setup. A sequence-to-sequence task on a finite vocabulary of tokens <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is associated with an input distribution <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> over the input <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}\subseteq\Sigma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}\subseteq\Sigma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a target function <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\Sigma^{*}\rightarrow\Sigma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\Sigma^{*}\rightarrow\Sigma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> for some model class <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>.
A composite task with the target function <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{H}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{H}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> can consist of <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> steps <math id="A3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1},f_{2},\dots,f_{T}\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1},f_{2},\dots,f_{T}\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="A3.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(x)=f_{T}\circ\cdots\circ f_{2}\circ f_{1}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=f_{T}\circ\cdots\circ f_{2}\circ f_{1}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For simplicity, assume <math id="A3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, and it includes the identity mapping so that <math id="A3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}\subseteq\mathcal{H}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}\subseteq\mathcal{H}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Now we present the detailed proofs for our theoretical results.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the case when <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> composite task examples <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{0}=\{(x_{i},y_{i}):i\in[k_{c}]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{0}=\{(x_{i},y_{i}):i\in[k_{c}]\}</annotation></semantics></math> are given, where <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. from <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}=f(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}=f(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{H}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{H}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3</span></span><span id="Thmproposition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Restatement of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Can Language Models Compose Skills In-Context?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)<span id="Thmproposition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists a learning rule <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}:(\mathcal{X}\times\Sigma^{*})^{*}\rightarrow\Sigma^{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}:(\mathcal{X}\times\Sigma^{*})^{*}\rightarrow\Sigma^{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any distribution <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{H}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{H}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, for every <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\delta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\delta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have with probability at least <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}[\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{S}_{0})(x)\neq f(x)]\leq\frac{1}{k_{c}}\left(T\ln|\mathcal{H}|+\ln\left(\frac{1}{\delta}\right)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>ln</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}[\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{S}_{0})(x)\neq f(x)]\leq\frac{1}{k_{c}}\left(T\ln|\mathcal{H}|+\ln\left(\frac{1}{\delta}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The result follows a standard argument of consistent models from a finite hypothesis class.
Let <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{S}_{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{S}_{c})</annotation></semantics></math> output a consistent model:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{S}_{c})\in\{g\in\mathcal{H}^{T}:g(x)=y,\forall(x,y)\in\mathcal{S}_{c}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{S}_{c})\in\{g\in\mathcal{H}^{T}:g(x)=y,\forall(x,y)\in\mathcal{S}_{c}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d(f,g)=\Pr_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}[g(x)\neq f(x)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(f,g)=\Pr_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}[g(x)\neq f(x)]</annotation></semantics></math> denote the difference between <math id="A3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>. For a fixed <math id="A3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(f,g)&gt;\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(f,g)&gt;\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr[g(x)=y,\forall(x,y)\in\mathcal{S}_{c}]\leq(1-\epsilon)^{k_{c}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr[g(x)=y,\forall(x,y)\in\mathcal{S}_{c}]\leq(1-\epsilon)^{k_{c}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">So</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr[\exists g\in\mathcal{H}^{T},g(x)=y,\forall(x,y)\in\mathcal{S}_{c}]\leq|\mathcal{H}^{T}|(1-\epsilon)^{k_{c}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr[\exists g\in\mathcal{H}^{T},g(x)=y,\forall(x,y)\in\mathcal{S}_{c}]\leq|\mathcal{H}^{T}|(1-\epsilon)^{k_{c}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Letting the right-hand side bounded by <math id="A3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> leads to the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Next we consider examples from multiple tasks. Recall that <math id="A3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a set of <math id="A3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> examples from the <math id="A3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th task <math id="A3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{D}_{t},f_{t})(0\leq t\leq T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{D}_{t},f_{t})(0\leq t\leq T)</annotation></semantics></math>. We say <math id="A3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">focusing</em> if its expected error on the <math id="A3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>-th task is no worse than that on any other task, i.e., for any <math id="A3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{0}(\mathcal{M};(\mathcal{D}_{t},f_{t})_{t=0}^{T})\leq\mathcal{L}_{j}(\mathcal{M};(\mathcal{D}_{t},f_{t})_{t=0}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{0}(\mathcal{M};(\mathcal{D}_{t},f_{t})_{t=0}^{T})\leq\mathcal{L}_{j}(\mathcal{M};(\mathcal{D}_{t},f_{t})_{t=0}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p5.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{j}(\mathcal{M};(\mathcal{D}_{t},f_{t})_{t=0}^{T}):=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{S}_{t}\sim(\mathcal{D}_{t},f_{t}),0\leq t\leq T}\Pr_{x\sim\mathcal{D}_{j}}[\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{S}_{0};\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T})(x)\neq f_{j}(x)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{j}(\mathcal{M};(\mathcal{D}_{t},f_{t})_{t=0}^{T}):=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{S}_{t}\sim(\mathcal{D}_{t},f_{t}),0\leq t\leq T}\Pr_{x\sim\mathcal{D}_{j}}[\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{S}_{0};\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T})(x)\neq f_{j}(x)]</annotation></semantics></math> is the expected error of <math id="A3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> on the <math id="A3.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th task. And we say that <math id="A3.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> does <em id="A3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not distinguish examples from different tasks</em>, if it is symmetric w.r.t. the data sets <math id="A3.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>’s, i.e., for any permutation <math id="A3.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1,\ldots,T\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1,\ldots,T\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the distribution of <math id="A3.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(0)};\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(1)},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(T)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(0)};\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(1)},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(T)})</annotation></semantics></math> is the same as that of <math id="A3.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{S}_{0};\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{S}_{0};\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4</span></span><span id="Thmproposition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Restatement of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Can Language Models Compose Skills In-Context?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>)<span id="Thmproposition4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose there exist <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{1},\ldots,g_{T}\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{1},\ldots,g_{T}\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> with pairwise difference at least <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\min_{i\neq j}\Pr_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}[g_{i}(x)\neq g_{j}(x)]\geq\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{i\neq j}\Pr_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}[g_{i}(x)\neq g_{j}(x)]\geq\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> that is focusing but does not distinguish between examples from different tasks, there exist <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1},\ldots,f_{T}\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1},\ldots,f_{T}\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f_{0}=f_{T}\circ\cdots f_{2}\circ f_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{0}=f_{T}\circ\cdots f_{2}\circ f_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{t}(0\leq t\leq T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{t}(0\leq t\leq T)</annotation></semantics></math>’s, such that
<math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\Pr_{x\sim\mathcal{D}_{0}}[\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{S}_{0};\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T})(x)\neq f_{0}(x)]=\Omega(\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\Pr_{x\sim\mathcal{D}_{0}}[\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{S}_{0};\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T})(x)\neq f_{0}(x)]=\Omega(\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}=g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}=g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{t}=\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{t}=\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>.
For datasets <math id="A3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{0},\mathcal{V}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{V}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{0},\mathcal{V}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{V}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and a task <math id="A3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{D}_{j},f_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{D}_{j},f_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{V}_{0},\mathcal{V}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{V}_{T};\mathcal{D}_{j},f_{j}):=\Pr_{x\sim\mathcal{D}_{j}}[\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{V}_{0};\mathcal{V}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{V}_{T})(x)\neq f_{j}(x)]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{V}_{0},\mathcal{V}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{V}_{T};\mathcal{D}_{j},f_{j}):=\Pr_{x\sim\mathcal{D}_{j}}[\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{V}_{0};\mathcal{V}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{V}_{T})(x)\neq f_{j}(x)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider a uniform distribution <math id="A3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> over permutations on <math id="A3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1,\ldots,T\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1,\ldots,T\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\mathbb{E}_{\sigma\sim\mathcal{U}}\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(0)},\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(1)},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(T)};\mathcal{D}_{\sigma(0)},f_{\sigma(0)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\mathbb{E}_{\sigma\sim\mathcal{U}}\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(0)},\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(1)},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(T)};\mathcal{D}_{\sigma(0)},f_{\sigma(0)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\sigma\sim\mathcal{U}}\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{0},\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T};\mathcal{D}_{\sigma(0)},f_{\sigma(0)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\sigma\sim\mathcal{U}}\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{0},\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T};\mathcal{D}_{\sigma(0)},f_{\sigma(0)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T+1}\sum_{t=0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{0},\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T};\mathcal{D},f_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T+1}\sum_{t=0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{0},\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T};\mathcal{D},f_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first equation comes from the assumption that <math id="A3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> does not distinguish between examples from different tasks, and the second equation is because <math id="A3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly at random. We have the following triangle inequality about the error by definition:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmclaim1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmclaim1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 1</span></span><span id="Thmclaim1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmclaim1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmclaim1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmclaim1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmclaim1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{0},\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T};\mathcal{D},f_{i})+\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{0},\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T};\mathcal{D},f_{j})\geq\Pr_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}[f_{i}(x)\neq f_{j}(x)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{0},\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T};\mathcal{D},f_{i})+\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{0},\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T};\mathcal{D},f_{j})\geq\Pr_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}[f_{i}(x)\neq f_{j}(x)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\mathbb{E}_{\sigma\sim\mathcal{U}}\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(0)},\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(1)},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(T)};\mathcal{D}_{\sigma(0)},f_{\sigma(0)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\mathbb{E}_{\sigma\sim\mathcal{U}}\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(0)},\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(1)},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(T)};\mathcal{D}_{\sigma(0)},f_{\sigma(0)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T+1}\sum_{t=0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{0},\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T};\mathcal{D},f_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T+1}\sum_{t=0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{0},\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T};\mathcal{D},f_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{T(T+1)}\sum_{t=1}^{T}T\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{0},\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T};\mathcal{D},f_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{T(T+1)}\sum_{t=1}^{T}T\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{0},\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T};\mathcal{D},f_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T(T+1)}\sum_{i=1}^{T}\sum_{j=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{0},\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T};\mathcal{D},f_{i})+\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{0},\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T};\mathcal{D},f_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T(T+1)}\sum_{i=1}^{T}\sum_{j=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{0},\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T};\mathcal{D},f_{i})+\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{0},\mathcal{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{T};\mathcal{D},f_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{T(T+1)}\sum_{i=1}^{T}\sum_{j=1}^{T}\Pr_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}[f_{i}(x)\neq f_{j}(x)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{T(T+1)}\sum_{i=1}^{T}\sum_{j=1}^{T}\Pr_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}[f_{i}(x)\neq f_{j}(x)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{T-1}{T+1}\Delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{T-1}{T+1}\Delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, since <math id="A3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is focusing,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(0)},\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(1)},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(T)};\mathcal{D}_{\sigma(0)},f_{\sigma(0)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\mathbb{E}_{\{\mathcal{S}_{t}\}}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M};\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(0)},\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(1)},\ldots,\mathcal{S}_{\sigma(T)};\mathcal{D}_{\sigma(0)},f_{\sigma(0)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}_{0}(\mathcal{M};(\mathcal{D}_{\sigma(t)},f_{\sigma(t)})_{t=0}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}_{0}(\mathcal{M};(\mathcal{D}_{\sigma(t)},f_{\sigma(t)})_{t=0}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{L}_{\sigma^{-1}(0)}(\mathcal{M};(\mathcal{D}_{\sigma(t)},f_{\sigma(t)})_{t=0}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{L}_{\sigma^{-1}(0)}(\mathcal{M};(\mathcal{D}_{\sigma(t)},f_{\sigma(t)})_{t=0}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
